  "result": "I've found one close match, terminal#9708, which is about keycap emoji rendering wrongly. I'm writing up the answer now.\n\n{\"seen_before\": true, \"matches\": [\"terminal#9708\"], \"answer\": \"This has been reported before. Keycap emoji such as 1️⃣ are made of several codepoints (digit, U+FE0F, U+20E3). Windows Terminal doesn't handle that sequence well, so the digit and the box are drawn misaligned. In terminal#9708 a maintainer ([user]) said keycap emojis are a special case that Windows doesn't support well. Fixing it needs custom detection logic in the font-fallback step (MapCharacters) of the text renderer. That ticket was still open as of September 2025, and I found no fix in the archive. There is no known setting that fixes it. Single-codepoint emoji such as 🔟 render correctly. You can follow or add your screenshots to terminal#9708. Related older tickets on multi-codepoint emoji and variation selectors are terminal#8970 and terminal#1472, but they were closed as duplicates.\"}",
